# What must never enter a Netwise image.
#
# THIS IS A PRIVACY BOUNDARY BEFORE IT IS A SIZE ONE.
#     `.gitignore` keeps real network configs out of the repository. An image
#     is a second way to distribute a file, and it does not consult
#     `.gitignore` -- `COPY . .` would put `configs/` and every submission
#     document into a layer that can be pushed to a registry.
#
#     The Dockerfile also copies named directories rather than `.` for the
#     same reason: two independent controls, because one of them will
#     eventually be edited by someone who does not know about the other.

# --- Real network data. Never. ---------------------------------------------
configs/
*.cfg
*.conf

# --- Personal identifiers and submission documents --------------------------
docs/
*.docx
*.pptx
*.pdf

# --- Local environment ------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Version control and CI -------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# --- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- The compose file does not belong inside the image it builds ------------
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
